{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0293"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c025): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c025.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0293"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge sport-games/olympics","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/sport-games__olympics.g3.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",1066],["+","Rome turned chariot racing into a mass entertainment and a professional career. In the Circus Maximus the drivers, not the owners, became the stars, and the most successful of them, Gaius Appuleius Diocles from Lusitania, won 1,462 of his 4,257 four-horse races between AD 122 and about 146 and retired with 35,863,120 sesterces in prize money – enough for some historians to call him the highest-paid athlete of all time.\n\n"],["=",73]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",1022],["+","Rom machte aus dem Wagenrennen eine Massenunterhaltung und einen Beruf. Im Circus Maximus wurden die Lenker, nicht die Besitzer, zu Stars, und der erfolgreichste von ihnen, Gaius Appuleius Diocles aus Lusitanien, gewann zwischen 122 und etwa 146 n. Chr. 1462 seiner 4257 Viergespann-Rennen und zog sich mit 35.863.120 Sesterzen Preisgeld zurück – genug, dass manche Historiker ihn den bestbezahlten Sportler aller Zeiten nennen.\n\n"],["=",81]]}]},
